\\ dissolve.6502 - the dissolve (the CPC's &1337, docs/cpc-text.md): its request and state, in main RAM for the
\\ intro, the stage's start and end and the game's end to ask for it; its step (dissolvestep.6502) in the data's
\\ bank, through dissolve_run.

SECTION GameVars
.DissolveIn                             ; bit 7 set for in
    SKIP 1
.DissolveMask                           ; the next mask
    SKIP 1
.DissolveLeft                           ; loops left (0 none): the CPC's &1766 = 2 while it isn't
    SKIP 1
ENDSECTION

\\ Start a dissolve (the CPC's &1337): its pattern 1-3 by a random number (AND 3, 0 taken as 1: the tables have
\\ it twice), out or in. It ends a page, as the CPC's (both are its &1766); a page asked for doesn't end it
\\ (the intro asks for its title every loop), and the game asks for none while one runs.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     A: bit 7 set for in
\\     Rng
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     the dissolve's state, Rng; PageOn 0
\\     C: clear
\\     A, X: corrupted; Z clear (DissolveLeft's load: 7 or 8)

.dissolve_start
{
    STA DissolveIn
    JSR random
    AND #3
    BIT DissolveIn:BPL @+
    ORA #4                              ; (in: from 4)
.@
    TAX                                 ; 0-7
    LDA #0:STA PageOn
    LDA DissolveFirst,X:STA DissolveMask
    LDA DissolveCount,X:STA DissolveLeft
    CLC                                 ; (for flow.6502's: a state's done)
    RTS
}

\\ A dissolve's step, if one's running (the CPC's &12CF with &1766 = 2): the data's bank paged in for it.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     the dissolve's state
\\     back
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     as dissolve_step's
\\     A, X, Y: corrupted

.dissolve_run
{
    LDA DissolveLeft:BEQ none
    LDX bankdata:STX &FE30              ; ROMSEL: the data's bank
    JSR dissolve_step
    LDX bankcode:STX &FE30              ; ROMSEL: the code's back
.none
    RTS
}

    INCLUDE "../build/gen/dissolvepat.6502" ; the patterns' first masks and loops (tools/gentext.py)
